#Carousel Architecture
Carousel Architecture are used in basically ui/ux making and database processing and —where items or tasks are processed in a continuous, repeating loop, just like a revolving merry-go-round
Instead of processing items in a single straight line from start to finish, the system keeps cycling through items, giving each a short turn, and moving to the next.
How it Works: Only 1 to 3 items are visible on screen at once, but in the background, all items are arranged in a circular loop. Swiping right or clicking "Next" smoothly cycles to the next item, wrapping back to the beginning when you reach the end.


